YBP1194 was considered a desirable destination for the [[Enterprise-class interstellar vehicle|first generation of warp ships.]] However, it would take another 30 years before NASA even began formally preparing for such a mission, due to the extreme distances involved. No spacecraft fitted with a the early generations of the White-Alcubierre Drive were capable of reaching YBP1194 in what NASA considered to be a reasonable amount of time. With so many desirable worlds far closer, NASA deferred the mission until the [[Falcon-class intstellar vehicle|Falcon-class interstellar vehicle]] began development in the 2080s. When the first Odysseus-series of probes started to enter production, NASA was given support by Congress to prepare a mission to YBP1194 c. On April 1, 2088 the probes Odysseus VIII, IX, X, and XI were launched toward YP1194 to chart a safe path for a crewed interstellar vehicle. The Odysseus IX and X were lost after the first 5 years, and the Odysseus VIII after 7 years. After 15 years, and 700 transits at warp, the Odysseus XI safely reached the YBP1194 system on July 4, 2103. 

Having only traveled half a light year on its last transit, Odysseus XI's Bubble Trap produced a relatively small blast of radiation visible as a twinkling star from the surface of Alo. By all accounts, this went unnoticed by the all but two amateur astronomers who were unable to identify a source. Their log entries identifying the light they saw would not be reported until after First Contact. Odysseus XI spent two years charting the planetary system and observing Alo, confirming the presence of intelligent life. Upon confirming the presence of an industrial civilization, NASA changed the flight schedule for the IV-402 Beagle III to conduct first contact.

==Pre-contact geopolitics==
Since the establishment of the Tilio'ramna Pact in 2047, power on Alo has been divided into 5 major supranational entities with varying degrees of integration of their member states. Only the city-state of X'anlio'ramna has remained unaffiliated and completely neutral since the start of this era, a consequence of it being located in the Tavurl Mountains and not easily accessible by any single power.

