The smallest of the blocs, and the only one to be completely landlocked. The CCMS is located in the interior of Osomi, and the majority of its territory is scrubland and desert, with most of its population centered on the south shore of the Lonli megalake. The CCMS has a largely cordial relationship with the Kuvo Republic, and through that is able to maintain favorable relations with the rest of the OC. It is the only non-nuclear supranational entity on Alo, and militarily its independence is maintained by the impassibility of its territory.

===First Contact===
IV-402 ''Beagle III'' departed the Sol System for the YBP1194 system on August 20, 2105 for a 7 year transit, a duration second only to the relief mission to [[Tel-ma]] beginning in 2091. On January 9, 2112 the ''Beagle III'' reached the edge of the YBP1194 system. Antimatter propulsion ceased on January 15, 2112, and construction of the YBP1194 [[Orbitals|Beachhead Orbital]] began on February 1. The crew of the ''Beagle III'' was completely awoken from suspended animation by March 3, 2112, and satellites manufactured from the Trojan asteroid and real-time data from Odysseus XI confirmed not only advanced industrial civilizations but large ground based observatories, which convinced NASA to issue an order to ''Beagle III'' to halt all plans for uncrewed landings and to instead prioritize First Contact-at-a-distance or radio First Contact on April 2, 2112. For the next year, the crew of the ''Beagle III'' would use their satellite network to tap into the radio and TV signals of the planet. They made no attempt to mask the presence of the satellites orbiting Alo, as it was assumed any civilization with ground based observatories on the scale of Alo's would have been able to spot an anti-matter driven spacecraft.

